{"ts": 1794243196.528, "request_id": "63febec9", "question": "What oxygen level allows steady flames in the BRE tests?", "params": {"psi": "PSI-20"}, "params_source": {"psi": "extracted"}, "scope": {"psis": ["PSI-20"], "n_psis": 1, "n_sources": 66, "n_chunks": 2701, "selected_by": {"psi": ["PSI-20"]}, "widened": false, "params_used": {"psi": "PSI-20"}}, "vector": [{"chunk_id": "ref:S6-REF-DIR-p31", "type": "text", "page": 31, "score": 0.6168}, {"chunk_id": "card:F-P2-33912767-1-0", "type": "text", "page": 2, "score": 0.5355}, {"chunk_id": "card:F-P2-0bf839ee-2-0", "type": "text", "page": 9, "score": 0.4865}, {"chunk_id": "ref:S6-REF-DIR-p36", "type": "text", "page": 36, "score": 0.4819}, {"chunk_id": "psi:PSI-20", "type": "text", "page": null, "score": 0.475}, {"chunk_id": "card:F-P2-7725dbd6-1-0", "type": "text", "page": 2, "score": 0.4662}, {"chunk_id": "card:F-P2-312dcc72-1-1", "type": "text", "page": 7, "score": 0.4629}, {"chunk_id": "card:F-P2-2e63b7c5-2-1", "type": "text", "page": 12, "score": 0.4583}, {"chunk_id": "card:F-P2-97aefb4a-2-1", "type": "text", "page": 8, "score": 0.4473}, {"chunk_id": "card:F-P2-2e63b7c5-2-0", "type": "text", "page": 12, "score": 0.4468}], "keyword": [{"chunk_id": "challenge:c9", "type": "text", "page": null, "score": 1.3}, {"chunk_id": "card:F-P2-2e63b7c5-2-0", "type": "text", "page": 12, "score": 0.7}, {"chunk_id": "challenge:c2", "type": "text", "page": null, "score": 0.7}, {"chunk_id": "card:F-P2-0bf839ee-2-0", "type": "text", "page": 9, "score": 0.6}, {"chunk_id": "card:F-P2-2e63b7c5-2-1", "type": "text", "page": 12, "score": 0.5}, {"chunk_id": "card:F-P2-33912767-2-2", "type": "text", "page": 7, "score": 0.5}, {"chunk_id": "ref:S6-REF-DIR-p31", "type": "text", "page": 31, "score": 0.5}, {"chunk_id": "psi:PSI-20", "type": "text", "page": null, "score": 0.5}, {"chunk_id": "card:F-P2-33912767-1-0", "type": "text", "page": 2, "score": 0.4}, {"chunk_id": "card:F-P2-97aefb4a-2-1", "type": "text", "page": 8, "score": 0.4}], "reranked": [{"chunk_id": "ref:S6-REF-DIR-p31", "score": 0.0163, "text": "Generally, it has been found that oxygen levels of 26 % and above can allow steady flames."}, {"chunk_id": "card:F-P2-33912767-1-0", "score": 0.016, "text": "In the first round of the BRE (Flamenco) experiment, it has been observed that the flames are long-living and quasi steady if the ambient oxygen mole fraction is above 0.265.\nEvidence: On the ISS, the"}, {"chunk_id": "card:F-P2-0bf839ee-2-0", "score": 0.0159, "text": "Normal Earth oxygen conditions will support burning with an added heat flux of 7 kW/m2.\nContext: While the oxygen levels below 0.265 do not support the theoretical steady burning of PMMA, there will b"}, {"chunk_id": "psi:PSI-20", "score": 0.0154, "text": "Burning Rate Emulator (BRE) (PSI-20), flight experiment. ACME / Burning Rate Emulator (BRE) Hardware: ACME. Fuel: Gas emulating solids: CH4/N2, C2H4/N2 on 25/50 mm porous burners. Key conditions: 14.7"}, {"chunk_id": "ref:S6-REF-DIR-p36", "score": 0.0148, "text": "All these image sequences suggest that higher oxygen, lower pressure, and lower heats of combustion tend to generate more stable flames that could reach steady state or last longer."}], "composer": {"provider": "extractive", "model": null, "key": null, "fallback_reason": "gemini: TimeoutError; groq: TimeoutError; ", "sentences": [{"text": "Generally, it has been found that oxygen levels of 26 % and above can allow steady flames.", "chunks": [1], "kept": true, "reason": "extractive fallback (gemini: TimeoutError; groq: TimeoutError; )"}]}, "outcome": "answer", "latency_ms": {"scope": 0, "search": 2335, "search_embed": 529, "search_db": 128, "search_vector": 124, "search_keyword": 126, "search_rerank": 1678, "compose": 1467, "total": 3803}, "keys": {"embed": "cohere#1", "composer": null}, "path": "rag", "reranker": "rrf (rerank unavailable)", "outcome_reason": ""}
{"ts": 1794243200.35, "request_id": "3ea6e787", "question": "Why are flames round in space?", "params": {}, "params_source": {}, "scope": {"psis": [], "n_psis": 0, "n_sources": null, "n_chunks": null, "selected_by": {}, "widened": false, "params_used": {}}, "vector": [{"chunk_id": "card:F-P2-e01ead6e-2-2", "type": "text", "page": 9, "score": 0.558}, {"chunk_id": "card:F-P2-2e63b7c5-2-0", "type": "text", "page": 12, "score": 0.5151}, {"chunk_id": "card:F-P2-e01ead6e-2-1", "type": "text", "page": 9, "score": 0.5063}, {"chunk_id": "card:F-P2-33912767-2-1", "type": "text", "page": 7, "score": 0.5025}, {"chunk_id": "card:F-P2-c2b84640-1-1", "type": "text", "page": 10, "score": 0.4934}, {"chunk_id": "card:F-P2-93993f05-1-0", "type": "text", "page": 3, "score": 0.4895}, {"chunk_id": "card:F-P2-ddd889ad-1-0", "type": "text", "page": 4, "score": 0.487}, {"chunk_id": "card:F-P2-648aaa91-2-1", "type": "text", "page": 11, "score": 0.4843}, {"chunk_id": "card:F-P1-159-cards-2-0", "type": "text", "page": 1, "score": 0.4819}, {"chunk_id": "card:F-P2-9f30ccd0-2-0", "type": "text", "page": 11, "score": 0.4721}], "keyword": [{"chunk_id": "psi:PSI-142", "type": "text", "page": null, "score": 1.2}, {"chunk_id": "psi:PSI-10", "type": "text", "page": null, "score": 1.1}, {"chunk_id": "psi:PSI-21", "type": "text", "page": null, "score": 1.1}, {"chunk_id": "psi:PSI-23", "type": "text", "page": null, "score": 1.0}, {"chunk_id": "psi:PSI-107", "type": "text", "page": null, "score": 1.0}, {"chunk_id": "psi:PSI-62", "type": "text", "page": null, "score": 1.0}, {"chunk_id": "psi:PSI-106", "type": "text", "page": null, "score": 0.8}, {"chunk_id": "psi:PSI-159", "type": "text", "page": null, "score": 0.8}, {"chunk_id": "psi:PSI-25", "type": "text", "page": null, "score": 0.8}, {"chunk_id": "psi:PSI-117", "type": "text", "page": null, "score": 0.7}], "reranked": [{"chunk_id": "card:F-P2-e01ead6e-2-2", "score": 0.0156, "text": "Unlike earlier flight-based experiments in this series during flights STS-83 and STS-94, excessive radiative heat losses, leading to quenching of the flame tip and tip-opening behavior, did not occur "}, {"chunk_id": "card:F-P2-2e63b7c5-2-0", "score": 0.0153, "text": "The BRE burner tests at NASA Glenn's 5.18-s Zero Gravity Research Facility showed that the flames were nearly hemispherical within 5 s, with the flame height still increasing.\nContext: The BRE burner,"}, {"chunk_id": "card:F-P2-e01ead6e-2-1", "score": 0.0151, "text": "The characteristic development time of the flame illustrated in Fig. 2 is only 14.3 ms.\nEvidence: In an experiment of a type the paper does not state, the authors report."}, {"chunk_id": "card:F-P2-33912767-2-1", "score": 0.0148, "text": "The buoyancy-driven velocity results in a much shorter residence time (about 0.04 s) in normal gravity than that estimated for microgravity flames.\nContext: At the same time, such flame generates the "}, {"chunk_id": "card:F-P2-c2b84640-1-1", "score": 0.0146, "text": "Extinction radius roughly scales with flow rate raised to the 0.4 power.\nEvidence: In a drop-tower test, the authors report."}], "composer": {"provider": "gemini", "model": "gemini-3.5-flash-lite", "key": "gemini#2", "fallback_reason": "", "sentences": []}, "outcome": "not_found", "latency_ms": {"scope": 0, "search": 2185, "search_embed": 358, "search_db": 140, "search_vector": 137, "search_keyword": 138, "search_rerank": 1687, "compose": 944, "total": 3129}, "keys": {"embed": "cohere#2", "composer": "gemini#2"}, "rewritten_query": "Why are flames round in space? spherical flame shape buoyancy microgravity", "reason": "the composer found no answer in the excerpts", "path": "rag", "reranker": "rrf (rerank unavailable)", "outcome_reason": "the composer found no answer in the excerpts"}
