, "page": 9, "score": 0.1}, {"chunk_id": "card:F-P2-4060cc43-1-0", "type": "text", "page": 7, "score": 0.1}], "reranked": [{"chunk_id": "doc:1a9f86ed7a47:p2:f7", "score": 0.436, "text": "[Figure] U.S. astronaut Ricky Arnold conducting CIR maintenance tasks.\nEDUCATION: https://tinyurl.com/space-flames CONTACT: Dennis Stocker, NASA Glenn Research Center, ACME Project Scientist, 216-433-"}, {"chunk_id": "doc:4c4693c96ee4:p222:c3", "score": 0.1387, "text": "Title: Leakage of Water Cooling System Description: Leaks in the ACME Chamber Insert Assembly water lines results in damage to hardware or inadvertently contaminates the vacuum exhaust system. Excessi"}, {"chunk_id": "doc:c2628e781402:p1:f4", "score": 0.1044, "text": "[Figure] U.S. astronaut Ricky Arnold carrying out CIR maintenance tasks during CLD Flame experiment operations.\npectively led by Profs. Marshall Long (Yale University), Derek Dunn-Rankin (University o"}, {"chunk_id": "doc:8a53e0cfe5ab:p19:c7", "score": 0.0889, "text": "We want to acknowledge the invaluable assistance of the International Space Station crew in obtaining these research results. Their meticulous operation and observations during the testing contributed"}, {"chunk_id": "doc:5fe67fa75841:p18:c4", "score": 0.0888, "text": "The CIR experiments are configured, but not conducted, by the ISS crew. Thus far, ACME's activity has included the majority of the crew members, regardless of their nationalities. Most often the astro"}], "composer": {"sentences": []}, "outcome": "clarify", "latency_ms": {"scope": 3, "search": 949, "search_embed": 341, "search_db": 124, "search_vector": 124, "search_keyword": 36, "search_rerank": 483, "total": 1018}, "keys": {"embed": "cohere#4"}, "path": "rag", "clarify": {"question": "Which do you mean: ACME BRE (PSI-20), BASS-II (PSI-25) or ACME CFI-G (PSI-159)?", "options": ["ACME BRE (PSI-20)", "BASS-II (PSI-25)", "ACME CFI-G (PSI-159)"], "why": "best rerank score 0.44 is below 0.65"}, "reranker": "cohere", "outcome_